---
import { RELEASES_URL, REPO_URL } from "../../lib/site";

/** Everything here must match apps/extension/build.mjs (the manifest) and release.yml. */
const WORKFLOW_URL = `${REPO_URL}/blob/main/.github/workflows/release.yml`;
const ATTEST = "gh attestation verify watchsync-extension.zip -R SuhaasNv/watchsync";
const commands = [
  { os: "Mac", where: "in Terminal", cmd: "shasum -a 256 ~/Downloads/watchsync-extension.zip" },
  {
    os: "Windows",
    where: "in Command Prompt or PowerShell",
    cmd: "certutil -hashfile Downloads\\watchsync-extension.zip SHA256",
  },
  { os: "Linux", where: "in a terminal", cmd: "sha256sum ~/Downloads/watchsync-extension.zip" },
];
---

<section class="safe" id="safe" aria-labelledby="safe-title">
  <h2 id="safe-title">Is it <span class="em">safe?</span></h2>
  <p class="intro">
    You're installing WatchSync from outside the Chrome Web Store, so Google hasn't reviewed it.
    Here is everything it can reach, what it never does, and how to check the file yourself.
  </p>

  <div class="pair">
    <div class="block">
      <h3>What it can reach</h3>
      <ul class="can">
        <li>
          <strong>Storage in your browser.</strong> Your name, and your room for up to 24 hours so
          you can rejoin after a restart.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>The WatchSync room service</strong> at <code>join.watchsync.space</code>, to send
          play, pause and the position to your room, and to open invite links.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Netflix, Prime Video and JioHotstar pages.</strong> It reads whether the video is
          playing, where it is and which title is open, applies play, pause and jumps from your room,
          and shows small notices on the player.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>GitHub, at most once a day</strong>, to see whether a newer version is out.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p class="note">
        That's the whole list. Its permissions are in <code>manifest.json</code>, in the folder
        you unzip, and the code that uses them is public.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="block">
      <h3>What it never does</h3>
      <ul class="never">
        <li>Read the picture, the sound or the rest of the page</li>
        <li>See your passwords, payments or account details</li>
        <li>Read your browsing history, or run on any other site</li>
        <li>Load code from the internet: everything it runs is in the zip</li>
        <li>Track you: no analytics, no ads, no cookies</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="note"><a href="/privacy/">Read the privacy notice</a></p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="pair">
    <div class="block">
      <h3>How the zip is made</h3>
      <p>
        All of WatchSync's code is <a href={REPO_URL} rel="noopener">public on GitHub</a>. Each
        release zip is built by GitHub Actions from a tagged commit on the main branch, using a <a
          href={WORKFLOW_URL}
          rel="noopener">public workflow</a
        >, and published on <a href={RELEASES_URL} rel="noopener">GitHub Releases</a>. The notes of
        every release name the commit and link to the build.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="block">
      <h3>Why Chrome shows a warning</h3>
      <p>
        Chrome shows a banner about developer-mode extensions for every extension that didn't come
        from the Chrome Web Store. It's about where the extension came from, not something Chrome
        found in it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="block check" id="check">
    <h3>Check your download</h3>
    <ol>
      <li>
        <p>
          Find the SHA-256 of the release: it's next to each download on the <a href="/releases/"
            >release notes</a
          > page, and in <code>SHA256SUMS.txt</code> on GitHub Releases.
        </p>
        <p class="latest" data-latest-sum hidden>
          <span>Latest, <span data-sum-version></span>:</span>{" "}
          <code data-sum></code>
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Ask your computer for the SHA-256 of the file you downloaded. If your browser renamed it,
          use that name.
        </p>
        <dl class="cmds">
          {
            commands.map((c) => (
              <div class="cmd">
                <dt>
                  {c.os} <span>{c.where}</span>
                </dt>
                <dd>
                  <code>{c.cmd}</code>
                  <button
                    class="btn copy"
                    type="button"
                    data-copy={c.cmd}
                    aria-label={`Copy the ${c.os} command`}
                  >
                    <span data-copy-label>Copy</span>
                  </button>
                </dd>
              </div>
            ))
          }
        </dl>
        <p>The two must match exactly. If they don't, don't install it, and tell us.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Optional, with the <a href="https://cli.github.com/" rel="noopener">GitHub CLI</a>
          (<code>gh</code>): this checks GitHub's signed record that our workflow built this exact
          file from our public code.
        </p>
        <div class="cmd solo">
          <code>{ATTEST}</code>
          <button
            class="btn copy"
            type="button"
            data-copy={ATTEST}
            aria-label="Copy the attestation command"
          >
            <span data-copy-label>Copy</span>
          </button>
        </div>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .safe {
    margin-top: clamp(32px, 5vw, 56px);
    padding: clamp(24px, 4vw, 44px);
    border-radius: 24px;
    background: var(--surface);
    box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--line);
  }
  h2 {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem);
    letter-spacing: -0.04em;
  }
  .intro {
    max-width: 40rem;
    margin-top: 12px;
    color: var(--text2);
    font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 1.5vw, 1.2rem);
  }
  .pair {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 0 clamp(24px, 4vw, 56px);
  }
  .block {
    margin-top: clamp(24px, 3vw, 36px);
    padding-top: 18px;
    box-shadow: inset 0 1px 0 var(--line2);
  }
  h3 {
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    font-weight: 750;
    letter-spacing: 0;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }
  p,
  li {
    color: var(--text2);
  }
  strong {
    color: var(--text);
  }
  a {
    color: var(--text);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  code {
    color: var(--text);
    background: var(--raised);
    padding: 0.1em 0.4em;
    border-radius: 6px;
    font-size: 0.92em;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }
  ul {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
    display: grid;
    gap: 10px;
  }
  ul li {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 26px;
  }
  ul li::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    left: 2px;
    top: 0.55em;
    width: 12px;
    height: 7px;
    border-left: 2px solid currentColor;
    border-bottom: 2px solid currentColor;
    transform: rotate(-45deg);
    color: var(--pres);
  }
  .never li::before {
    top: 0.75em;
    height: 0;
    border-left: 0;
    transform: none;
    color: var(--warn);
  }
  .note {
    margin-top: 14px;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }
  .note a {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    min-height: 44px;
  }
  .check ol {
    display: grid;
    gap: 22px;
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 1.4em;
  }
  .check li::marker {
    color: var(--acc);
    font-family: var(--display);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .check li > p + p,
  .check li > p + .cmds,
  .check li > .cmds + p,
  .check li > p + .cmd {
    margin-top: 10px;
  }
  .latest {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 6px 10px;
    align-items: baseline;
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
  }
  .latest[hidden] {
    display: none;
  }
  .cmds {
    display: grid;
    gap: 12px;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .cmds dt {
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--text);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }
  .cmds dt span {
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text2);
  }
  .cmds dd {
    margin: 4px 0 0;
  }
  .cmds dd,
  .cmd.solo {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 10px;
  }
  .cmds code,
  .cmd.solo code {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    min-height: 44px;
    padding: 6px 14px;
    border-radius: 10px;
    background: var(--bg);
    box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--line2);
    font-size: 0.88rem;
  }
  .copy {
    min-height: 44px;
    min-width: 6.5rem;
    padding: 0 16px;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }
  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .pair {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
